# Git and CI

- Conventional commits scoped by capability: `feat(index): add chromadb ingestion`,
  `test(eval): add recall@k harness`, `fix(data-quality): keep legacy Human Rights v1 indexed`.
- One feature branch per capability (`feat/chunking`, `feat/hybrid-search`), merged to `main`
  once tests pass. No force-push to `main`.
- Never commit `.venv/`, `.env`, `chroma/` persistence dirs, or model caches.
- CI: Python 3.11+, cache pip, `ruff check`, `mypy src`,
  `pytest -m "not integration and not llm"` on every push. That job already
  runs the eval harness tests and checks `eval/record.json`. MiniLM, the
  cross-encoder, and a live LLM live in `.github/workflows/extras.yml`
  (`workflow_dispatch` only) so they never appear as skipped on a PR.
  Fail the build on any error.
